# Vue Project Code Style and Organization Rules

## Component Structure
- Use Vue 3 Composition API with <script setup> syntax for better type inference and performance
- Break down components into smaller, reusable pieces when they exceed 200 lines
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility
- Use TypeScript for better type safety and developer experience

## File Organization
- Place reusable components in `src/components/`
- Place page-specific components in `src/pages/{PageName}/components/`
- Group related features in feature-based folders
- Keep all interfaces and types in separate `.ts` files under `src/types/`

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow utility-first approach
- Extract common style patterns into reusable classes
- Use @apply directive for complex, repeated utility combinations
- Maintain consistent spacing and sizing using Tailwind's scale

## Best Practices
- Use props validation with proper TypeScript types
- Implement proper error handling and loading states
- Use computed properties for derived state
- Avoid direct DOM manipulation
- Use refs instead of reactive for primitive values
- Implement proper cleanup in onUnmounted hooks

## Performance
- Use v-show instead of v-if for frequently toggled elements
- Implement proper key attributes in v-for loops
- Avoid expensive operations in template expressions
- Use shallowRef for large objects that don't need deep reactivity
- Implement virtual scrolling for long lists

## State Management
- Use provide/inject for shallow component trees
- Consider Pinia for complex state management
- Keep state mutations centralized and predictable
- Implement proper state hydration strategies

## Security
- Sanitize all user inputs
- Avoid v-html unless absolutely necessary
- Use proper CORS policies
- Implement proper authentication and authorization
- Never expose sensitive information in client-side code

## Testing
- Write unit tests for complex components
- Implement integration tests for critical user flows
- Use Vue Test Utils for component testing
- Maintain high test coverage for critical paths

## Code Style
- Use consistent naming conventions (PascalCase for components, camelCase for properties)
- Follow Vue's style guide priority A and B rules
- Use meaningful component and variable names
- Keep methods short and focused
- Document complex logic with comments

## Build and Development
- Use Vite for fast development experience
- Implement proper code splitting
- Optimize asset loading
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Maintain proper dependency management
